A||||12||Jasons85GT||Running out of solutions...and money! :(  Please help...||||9||
Z||000000||Jasons85GT||12-04-2001||06:04 PM||||Hey guys, I can't seem to figure out the problem, so I thought I'd ask yall...<P>Problem: One night I was out driving around and came to a stop light. Check engine light came on, then the car died. Started right back up, but kept acting like it wanted to die unless I gassed it. After 2 min or so, it ran fine. Got home, checked code, said it was the EGR. This happens several more times through the course of two weeks. Then, i noticed the idle began to "hunt" really bad, and the warmer the engine got, the lower it would go. Coming home from work on night, the RPMS started jumping up and down and the car was surging, so I came to a stop and it stalled. Started it back up, runs fine. Checked codes when I got home, this time it said TPS. During all this I noticed I have been getting poor gas milege. Finally, I started replacing stuff....<P>Things I've replaced: <BR>1) IAC<BR>2) TPS<BR>3) Controle module (under distributor)<BR>4) Distributor and rotor<BR>5) EGR valve<P>..........And after all that, NOTHING changed!! It hasn't stalled anymore, but the idle still "hunts" and gets lower and lower as the car warms up. (About 500-600 RPMS, and sometimes almost dies when I put it into Drive) And its still throwing the EGR code. I dont know what to do anymore. Im only 17 and not too mechanically inclined. Someone told me that my timing could be off....this true?? If so, what do I do?? (Dont laugh) I do have a job, but this car is making me go broke, which really bothers me cuz I love the car!! Any ideas anyone?? Please help if you can. Any replies are appreciated! Thanks...........'85 GT 2.8 Automatic<BR>||||reg||9
Z||000001||80's BOY||12-04-2001||06:07 PM||||here's an idea!! buy a V8 kit. read my post.||||reg||12
Z||000002||StuGood||12-04-2001||06:19 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jasons85GT:<BR><B>Someone told me that my timing could be off....this true??....'85 GT 2.8 Automatic</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE>It <B>is</B> possible the ignition timing is off... maybe because the timing chain slipped a notch as you approached the stop light.  Find someone with a timing light that knows what they're doing, follow the procedure on the underhood emissions sticker.  That would be my first step.<P>||||reg||3
Z||000003||Pyric||12-04-2001||06:25 PM||||Also you might want to check out the EGR tube.  It leads to the underside of the manifold.  It caused mine to hunt and it made the exhaust manifolds glow cherry red. <BR>Check your engine at night... You might see yours doing the same thing.||||reg||1
